Z||000000||four50four||10-17-1999||06:35 PM||||when people try to rip other people off when selling their fieros. i know everyone's fiero is worth a million dollars to themselves, but when some guy is asking $7,750 for a 86 gt, somethings wrong. thats over 10 grand canadian. it seems these people come to our forum to try and rip us off, then never post again. one such person that sticks out in my mind was Nick. i don't mean to pick on him, but he wanted something like $6000 for his 86 gt. that's just too much. well he was a honda guy anyway, but when i go to the mall and see a running 86 gt for $900 and antoher one for $7750, it makes me mad. the guy even says the price is lowered. a real fiero owner doesn't try to rip fellow fiero owners off.  i don't know if anyone else feels this way, but this sort of thing really ticks me off.||||reg||8
Z||000001||hefty||10-17-1999||07:14 PM||||What gets me going is small minded a**holes. I was just on exite auto chat and couldn't believe it. Muscle cars are cool, but I'd love to see a 400hp chevelle or other quarter miler hang with a Fiero in the curves. Don't bash a ride because it's not what you have, appreciate 'em all, I've worked on a huge varity of 'em, they all have pluses and minuses.<p>[This message has been edited by hefty (edited 10-17-1999).]||||reg||1
