Z||000004||2M4 Dale||10-17-1999||11:46 PM||||I think anyone who takes the time to care for their "ride" should be appreciated along with their auto of choice. I own a Fiero and a 66 Bonneville. I have also owned seven different GTOs a 71 Challenger and a 69 Ford XL460. I loved them all. Sure there are cars I'm not interested in but I sure won't knock them. The guys out there putting off on Fieros have probably never even ridden in one. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||superXmotorsports||10-17-1999||11:55 PM||||I own 5 fieros.  Price range $150 - $7000.<BR>I have seen GT's advertised for 10 and 12 grand (US) but they are 1 owner cars with 5 or 10K on the meter.  If someone has a legitimate model it certainly could sell for that and not be a scam.  Just my 2 cents.<BR>By the way I have 2 Mitsubishi Eclipses too (99 Spyder and 95 GSX).||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierospeeder||10-17-1999||11:58 PM||||Im new to the group and i own a fiero 84', 74 beetle, im rebuilding, and a tbird turbo 87. But i noticed that theres a lot of people selling fieros or beatles a lot more then they are worth. The only reason should be if its low mileage and rust free, otherwise your joking.  A fiero pace car i would understand because its rare.  I got my fiero for 350, i put my share of money into it, and you expect that from a 15 year old car.  Just keep on searching for a car until you find a good price and theres always a chance its a good car.  heres a website if people are looking for cars. <A HREF="http://www.traderonline.com" TARGET=_blank>www.traderonline.com</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Patrick||10-18-1999||12:21 AM||||<BR>You can't knock anyone for trying to get as much money as they can when they sell something. However, having said that, this doesn't mean that it's alright to be deceitful and lie about the item. If someone hasn't done their homework and they pay too much, well, too bad. Nobody is forcing anyone of us to buy anyone else's goods, whether they be Fieros, houses, or widgets.<P>People really need to take some responsibility for their own actions, and not try to blame every problem on someone else.||||reg||4
