Z||000015||turbo86se||10-19-1999||09:47 PM||||How do you price a car you're trying to sell? What you paid for it? Or what you think it's worth? For instance, last winter I came across a nice red '88 Formula for sale here in SC. The interior was mint, many new parts. 189,000 miles on odometer. The owner said the engine was blown and wouldn't start. I bought the car for $350 with the intention of parting it out. I took it to my local Fiero-maniac mechanic, and after 30 minutes of charging the battery, the engine started right up and was driveable! After installing a full set of Fel-Pro gaskets, today the car is still running excellent. I signed the title over to my mechanic in exchange for a complete 3800 installation in my T-Top 88 coupe. what if I were to sell the car instead of trading it, what would I ask for it? It's certainly worth more than $350! ||||reg||1
